From accdc35372bae72d5f855e6db535d0bcf88ee764 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:17:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(indoor): close numerical wall contacts in exact routing
 cells

The exact routing compiler keeps every original IEEE wall coordinate, so a
partition that misses the neighbouring wall face by a floating-point residue
(1e-14 ft) left a sliver that the rational overlay treated as an opening.
nativeWalkingRegion now applies the documented native contact rule to the
strict wall barriers before their own door aperture is cut: a wall vertex
within 1e-7 ft of another wall's edge, strictly outside it, is inserted into
that edge (native-routing-contact-noding.ts). No coordinate moves, nothing is
buffered, material is only added, and gaps over 1e-7 ft, doors, openings,
holes, columns and reviewed patch walls are untouched. The rule version is
part of the native circulation geometry key and the private physical memo.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
